    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: July 27, 2026</p>

    <p>
      By creating a Spens account or using the service, you agree to these terms. They are
      deliberately short and readable — please take a moment to go through them.
    </p>

    <h2>1. The service</h2>
    <p>
      Spens is a personal pocket ledger: it lets you record transactions and track budgets, savings
      goals, debts and accounts, on your own or in shared spaces. Spens is published by David
      Dossou, acting as an individual. Contact:
      <a href="mailto:djidenou@hey.com">djidenou@hey.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. A tracking tool, not an advisor</h2>
    <p>
      Spens helps you see your money clearly, but it <strong>provides no financial advice, no
      investment advice, and no banking or payment services</strong>. Amounts, categories and
      analytics shown are based on what you enter; automated features (such as quick add) can make
      mistakes, and it is up to you to verify your data. Your financial decisions remain your own.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must provide a valid email address that only you can access: it is used to sign you in with one-time codes.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for activity performed from your account. Let us know quickly if you suspect unauthorized access.</li>
      <li>The service is not intended for people under 15.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Shared spaces</h2>
    <p>
      When you invite someone into a shared space, or join one, the data in that space is visible to
      its members. Only record there what you are willing to share with them, and only invite people
      you trust.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use Spens for illegal or fraudulent purposes;</li>
      <li>attempt to access other users' data or compromise the security of the service;</li>
      <li>overload, probe or reverse-engineer the service, or scrape data from it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Serious violations may lead to suspension or deletion of your account.</p>

    <h2>6. Pricing</h2>
    <p>
      Spens is currently <strong>free</strong>. A paid tier may be introduced in the future for some
      features; core tracking features will remain accessible, and no switch to a paid plan will be
      imposed on you without clear prior notice. You will never be charged without your explicit
      consent.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      Your data belongs to you. How it is processed is described in the
      <%= link_to "privacy policy", privacy_path %>. You can delete your account at any time from
      your profile, which permanently erases your data.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Availability and liability</h2>
    <p>
      Spens is under active development and provided "as is". We do our best to keep it reliable and
